The project has the following objetives:

i) the upgrade of the connectivity for the Eastern regions surrounding Bogotá as the Project will represent a new North-South axis with shorter travel times for the departments of Meta, Cundinamarca and Boyacá, as well as metropolitan Bogota, benefiting a total population of approximately 300,000 inhabitants from the areas surrounding the Project; 
ii) the reduction in fuel consumption and consequently GHG emissions associated with decreased congestion in Bogota¿s metropolitan area; 
iii) The direct and indirect job creation during construction and operations, which are being estimated with the construction and operational teams.

The Project has the following objectives: 
a) together with the NHP toll road, it will create a direct connection between the capital and the Samaná peninsula;
b) it will reduce the travel time and distance between Santo Domingo and Samaná from 5-h to 1:45 h; 
c) it will allow for increased daily movement of visitors and tourists between Samaná and the Southern part of the island including the capital, and allow for a better connectivity with other touristic key spots such as Punta Cana; 
d) it will trigger economic development in the region by improving communications between producers, traders and final consumers in the Samaná peninsula, and also by engaging small and medium enterprises in services related with the Project during the construction and operation phases.

The end of the project is to improve the competitiveness of the agricultural sector in Ecuador, improving living conditions and working families who depend directly on the planting, cultivation and marketing of mangoes for export. 
The specific objectives of the project are: (i) Increase Ecuadorian mango exports to the markets of USA And the EU through the implementation of a program of Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) which allows standardize the quality of the fruit; (ii) Strengthening the chain of productive agricultural sector through the training of managers and staff of the estates that would improve the competitiveness of the sector and working conditions of staff; (iii) Achieve differentiation, and increase the competitiveness of the Ecuadorian mango in destination markets through the implementation of an export brand, identifying the product by its origin and quality;
(iv) Reduce the negative impact to the environment and the people in the mango is cultivated through the implementation of practices friendly and respectful of the environment that will enable the sustainability of crops ensuring jobs for the staff who depend on mangoes for their livelihood.

General objective: Create a Public-private partnership model to improve competitiveness and social-economic development of micro and potential employees of the Touristic Area Zona Rosa through training and microenterprise promotion of the Barrio Las Palmas population and conformation of a Business Improvement District

specific objectives: a) Awareness and promote the employability of youth and women's slum of Las Palmas to introduce jobs that demand is being generated in the area; 
b) To facilitate the incorporation of micro-targeting and sustainable incorporating into a population of the area and promoting its marginal chaining toward companies that are or are being established in the area; 
c) To form the structure of public private partnerships to maintain the sustainability of economic development in the area in an integrated manner through the formation of the Special Improvement District between the Association of Municipal Mayors-business-Ministries; 
d) Revitalization of infrastructure, lighting and beautification of some billboards in the Zona Rosa

The objectives of the operation are:
a) the construction of a third set of locks, including two lock complexes and watersaving basins at the Atlantic and Pacific ends of the Panama Canal (the "Canal");
b) the deepening of the Pacific and Atlantic entrances of the Canal;
c) the deepening and widening of the Canal's navigational channels, including the
Gaillard Cut; and
d) the raising of Gatun Lake to its maximum operational level.

The objective of the TC is to support the Bank's borrowing countries in the design of policies, regulations, planning processes and prioritization of investments in the air transport sector. 

The TC will finance the development of diagnostics, policy notes, methodologies, toolkits and pilot projects. The specific objectives include support to: 

(i) formulate policies that seek to increase regional and national air integration;
ii) design and implement mechanisms for the management, regulation and financing of infrastructure and airport services;
(iii) support adoption of technical and aviation safety standards; and 
(iv) acceleration of the adoption of aviation biofuels.

This program aims to consolidate the institution and regulatory framework for concessions in the transports sector, with the larger objective of fostering private sector participation in the provision and operation of the transports infrastructure in the state of Sao Paolo. The implementation of this program is also expected to have a demonstration effect in other states of the country to develop similar mechanisms. The program consists of four main components:
1) the consolidation of the institutional and regulatory framework for the concessions program and to strengthen the unit responsible for its administration;
2) preparation of specific studies concerning the concessions program; 
3) support to the Secretariat for Transports for the implementation of the concessions program; and 
4) interchange of experiences with other agencies implementing concessions programs.

The general objective of the project is to boost the competitiveness and productivity of private enterprises in three selected sectors through greater workforce efficiency. 
The specific objectives are to:
(a)encourage small and medium-sized businesses in the construction, tourism and wood processing sectors to invest in training for their employees;
(b) promote a better supply of training services in response to private sector demands; 
(c) generate experiences that can serve as best practice models for a future national occupational certification program.

The objective of the project is to strengthen the Superintendency so that it will be able to implement and enforce the new legal framework. To achieve this objective, the project will provide support in three areas:
(i) the drafting of the regulations for the new laws; 
(ii) the upgrading of supervision tools and practices and training of the inspectors and supervisors in consolidated supervision and;
(iii) strengthening of off-site supervision.

The proposed project will adapt the so-called accelerator model to Panama's market conditions. A Business Accelerator is commonly defined as an early stage venture capital company, investing in Interent infrastructure, software, telecommunications and other technology-related ventures. It provides tenants with strategy consulting, technology consulting, investment banking, and often venture capital through internal resources and global partner networks. 
This project will support the following activites to transform IDEP to a modified accelerator model: 
(i) developa new incubation mechanism with the high-tech workspace needed to service businesses in the New Economy;
 (ii) develop managerial, counselling and training services for client companies within the accelerator; 
(iii) support the proces of development of innovative ideas through a pre-incubation facility; and 
(iv) assist in the design of mechanisms for private sector financing for client companies and the accelerator.

The objective of the project is to consolidate and strengthen FIE as a leading provider of microfinancing services by improving and broadening the scope of these services for the benefit of its customers and the institution.
a. Hire specialized technical assistance for: (i) design new products, including credit for housing, rural credit operations for small population nuclei, and research and design a "smart card" (ii) market research for new areas (iii) develop a communications strategy and the strengthening of the institutional image, (iv) advise on long-term strategies, assessment of risk assets and improving operational mechanisms, (v) assist in attracting small savings, incentives personnel, and implementation of provisions of the Central Bank and SBEF, and (vi) update the "software" (change of platform) and developing modules for new products; 
b. Train key staff in managerial and operational level: (i) for managers / head offices and branches of analysis and interpretation of financial statements, budgetary and human resources management, (ii) to loan officers: evaluation, classification, placement and collection of receivables, (iii) for accountants: applying rules of SBEF and analysis and interpretation of financial statements, and (iv) specialized courses for cashiers in the current management, and computerized management of new products. The training will be done through different modalities, including timely events, seminars, workshops, and work with staff and external trainers.

The objective of the project is to facilitate the Microenterprise Financial Institutions of Latin America and the Caribbean (MFI) access to the private sources of capital, through the qualification of the associated risk of its operations, such as through the improved presentation of financial information. The specific objectives of the project are: to facilitate MFI's access to risk qualification and evaluation services; 
Develop the market for risk qualification for the MFI; provide continuous information to the market about the financial criteria of the industry.
The project will include the following three components: establish a "Rating Fund" to provide vouchers to microfinance institutions so that they can purchase rating services; create an "Information Exchange" on the web to provide a high degree of transparency to microfinance institutions; and promote and disseminate the project activities and results.

The general objective of the project is to strengthen the institutional and technical capacity of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs through the provision of negociating tools and assistance for the development, presentation and dissemination of information on the FTAA process. 
The specific objectives of the project are:
-Conduct studies on key trade issues with a view to strengthening Uruguay's participation in the final stage of the FTAA negociations;
-Conduct training, workshops designed to improve the capacity of negociators to articulate sound and technically rigorous negotiating positions;
-Design, construct and launch a Foreign Affairs Ministry webpage for the purpose of better communicating with civil society on issues surrounding trade and globalization; and
-Improve the information technology capabilities of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for the purpose of better participating in trade negotiations.
